{"versions":[{"path":"versions/f7fa496f-69e1-456f-8987-31f2313f62ad/3b0f6392a4eaf20be8cbcce8a7a6986faba446af089ec39f4c1e3cb926d25c5a.json","value":{"schema_version":1,"revision_scheme":"holly-question-v1","bank_id":"3eb3811b-4425-46ad-8bb6-a0504dca151b","question_id":"f7fa496f-69e1-456f-8987-31f2313f62ad","revision":"sha256:3b0f6392a4eaf20be8cbcce8a7a6986faba446af089ec39f4c1e3cb926d25c5a","kind":"mcqs","content":{"question":[{"type":"text","content":"Word stemming is to eliminate the commonly used words from the original documents."}],"options":[{"type":"text","content":"True","correct":false,"option_id":"a7aa7ca6-4711-4adc-8507-64cc28a9a670"},{"type":"text","content":"False","correct":true,"option_id":"4ddf18f7-eebf-40b5-9602-fcdcd2cbe1ff"}],"explanation":[{"type":"text","content":"词干提取把同源词的不同形式归并到词干, 如 connected 和 connecting 归并到 connect; 删除常用词属于停用词过滤"}]}}},{"path":"versions/f55f35dd-7769-49a0-a234-db520761a01c/7326fcc5c6f8e4570b68fccac358c0567d29eb9217c2e121060690f53d2c46e8.json","value":{"schema_version":3,"revision_scheme":"holly-question-v1","bank_id":"3eb3811b-4425-46ad-8bb6-a0504dca151b","question_id":"f55f35dd-7769-49a0-a234-db520761a01c","revision":"sha256:7326fcc5c6f8e4570b68fccac358c0567d29eb9217c2e121060690f53d2c46e8","kind":"mcqs","content":{"question":[{"type":"text","content":"A 2-3 tree with 12 leaves may have at most 11 nonleaf nodes."}],"options":[{"type":"text","content":"True","correct":false,"option_id":"f635b360-7738-4305-b758-4da11082eb75"},{"type":"text","content":"False","correct":false,"option_id":"67a933df-c4a8-40e1-8a32-51f2afd3b7cc"}],"explanation":[{"type":"text","content":"争议说明: at most 可表示非紧上界, 也可能指最大可达值, 存在歧义"}],"answer_status":"unavailable","selection_mode":"single"}}},{"path":"versions/4ad96974-c2d9-4163-bf13-97202efddade/7449b95b3bb29569989be7e7358fd3144e72ba8bc21c735c301d3db266cc2c9c.json","value":{"schema_version":1,"revision_scheme":"holly-question-v1","bank_id":"3eb3811b-4425-46ad-8bb6-a0504dca151b","question_id":"4ad96974-c2d9-4163-bf13-97202efddade","revision":"sha256:7449b95b3bb29569989be7e7358fd3144e72ba8bc21c735c301d3db266cc2c9c","kind":"mcqs","content":{"question":[{"type":"text","content":"For the document-partitioned strategy in distributed indexing, each node contains a subset of all documents that have a specific range of index."}],"options":[{"type":"text","content":"True","correct":true,"option_id":"dcc679bd-1ec5-4f3a-b4e8-0d9bcfd02e6b"},{"type":"text","content":"False","correct":false,"option_id":"f425dae1-19a1-4a52-995b-81e69eb41635"}],"explanation":[{"type":"text","content":"文档分片按文档编号或分配范围把文档集合分给不同节点, 每个节点为自己负责的文档构建索引"}]}}},{"path":"versions/b39abc85-67c5-4760-abcf-a8ab3fca299d/7b5b1e0adc901deb95e9bd685d8895b9a9bc058bb8dcc4672f5f776b69bb0ed5.json","value":{"schema_version":1,"revision_scheme":"holly-question-v1","bank_id":"3eb3811b-4425-46ad-8bb6-a0504dca151b","question_id":"b39abc85-67c5-4760-abcf-a8ab3fca299d","revision":"sha256:7b5b1e0adc901deb95e9bd685d8895b9a9bc058bb8dcc4672f5f776b69bb0ed5","kind":"mcqs","content":{"question":[{"type":"text","content":"In a red-black tree, the number of internal nodes in the subtree rooted at x is no more than 2^bh(x) − 1 where bh(x) is the black-height of x."}],"options":[{"type":"text","content":"True","correct":false,"option_id":"a89175d6-9f2e-4b27-b0bd-908a68d02472"},{"type":"text","content":"False","correct":true,"option_id":"be420bea-af89-4edc-9a0a-1a4294d964da"}],"explanation":[{"type":"text","content":"红黑树的标准引理是至少有 2^bh(x)−1 个内部结点, 这是下界. 例如黑根带两个红孩子的子树即可超过该下界"}]}}},{"path":"versions/cc28b8db-742c-4add-9a18-2939133ae4e7/b39a644037ad827e2a79750478bcb26798d8cc65bb7beeade2fd62427a8ec181.json","value":{"schema_version":1,"revision_scheme":"holly-question-v1","bank_id":"3eb3811b-4425-46ad-8bb6-a0504dca151b","question_id":"cc28b8db-742c-4add-9a18-2939133ae4e7","revision":"sha256:b39a644037ad827e2a79750478bcb26798d8cc65bb7beeade2fd62427a8ec181","kind":"mcqs","content":{"question":[{"type":"text","content":"When measuring the relevancy of the answer set, if the precision is high but the recall is low, it means that most of the relevant documents are retrieved, but too many irrelevant documents are returned as well."}],"options":[{"type":"text","content":"True","correct":false,"option_id":"cb2e67dd-837b-44aa-894a-f0a01ae6c59f"},{"type":"text","content":"False","correct":true,"option_id":"56d85355-255f-44d0-bfc9-68a18c2b4003"}],"explanation":[{"type":"text","content":"高 precision 表示检索到的文档中相关比例高; 低 recall 表示所有相关文档中只找回较小比例, 这与给出的解释相反"}]}}},{"path":"versions/96a744f1-fd34-4725-950f-f3f1d9e54b58/fd64ca79848a8403536bcfb971a68a9f99cabb17ac8309fa3cd6e87f143d2d35.json","value":{"schema_version":1,"revision_scheme":"holly-question-v1","bank_id":"3eb3811b-4425-46ad-8bb6-a0504dca151b","question_id":"96a744f1-fd34-4725-950f-f3f1d9e54b58","revision":"sha256:fd64ca79848a8403536bcfb971a68a9f99cabb17ac8309fa3cd6e87f143d2d35","kind":"mcqs","content":{"question":[{"type":"text","content":"For any black node X in a Red-Black tree, if it has two children, then the children's colors may be different."}],"options":[{"type":"text","content":"True","correct":true,"option_id":"ce893536-b734-4291-a710-01a60f849be7"},{"type":"text","content":"False","correct":false,"option_id":"d61e73e2-3fe2-48c2-af74-c42b294ffb07"}],"explanation":[{"type":"text","content":"可以让 X 的一个孩子是黑叶, 另一个孩子为红结点且具有两个黑孩子, 所有相关路径黑高相同, 红结点也无红孩子"}]}}},{"path":"versions/170fe444-90ed-4098-aabb-86eb221715d2/f2756cf9fa4e2d0cc44c0c8a68ef585d0af3bbb6bbf02b396bb80b9f289978ae.json","value":{"schema_version":1,"revision_scheme":"holly-question-v1","bank_id":"3eb3811b-4425-46ad-8bb6-a0504dca151b","question_id":"170fe444-90ed-4098-aabb-86eb221715d2","revision":"sha256:f2756cf9fa4e2d0cc44c0c8a68ef585d0af3bbb6bbf02b396bb80b9f289978ae","kind":"mcqs","content":{"question":[{"type":"text","content":"Inverted file contains a list of pointers to all occurrences of a term in the text."}],"options":[{"type":"text","content":"True","correct":true,"option_id":"84d3ec16-12f5-4d91-a9d3-69dbccd06e11"},{"type":"text","content":"False","correct":false,"option_id":"1dfc8bea-d2da-4671-9d96-d0edf84eac12"}],"explanation":[{"type":"text","content":"倒排文件为词项保存指向相关文档或出现位置的列表; 具体实现可能只保存文档级指针或额外保存位置"}]}}},{"path":"versions/13e7a761-83c9-4d38-81be-3c6ff12574d2/70e25797ab136d0bb98eda800db0a0d1919293960d620b148a62f9e9dd69788f.json","value":{"schema_version":1,"revision_scheme":"holly-question-v1","bank_id":"3eb3811b-4425-46ad-8bb6-a0504dca151b","question_id":"13e7a761-83c9-4d38-81be-3c6ff12574d2","revision":"sha256:70e25797ab136d0bb98eda800db0a0d1919293960d620b148a62f9e9dd69788f","kind":"mcqs","content":{"question":[{"type":"text","content":"The time bound of the FIND operation in a B+ tree containing N numbers is O(log N), no matter what the degree of the tree is."}],"options":[{"type":"text","content":"True","correct":true,"option_id":"b43177a9-208b-4a23-a74e-9bc70a31ecf7"},{"type":"text","content":"False","correct":false,"option_id":"89950f8e-8655-492e-803b-7f3cbb5a15a6"}],"explanation":[{"type":"text","content":"B+ 树保持平衡, 阶数为 M（M≥3）时树高为 $O(\\log_M N)$; 每层用二分查找需 $O(\\log M)$, 因此总查找时间为 $O(\\log N)$"}]}}},{"path":"versions/36808fb8-3493-45f3-b552-f90e6acfd1bb/1eedf6bc5cb41d790969612edfe7fc38445dd7881a07fd67731d2a26b2657575.json","value":{"schema_version":1,"revision_scheme":"holly-question-v1","bank_id":"3eb3811b-4425-46ad-8bb6-a0504dca151b","question_id":"36808fb8-3493-45f3-b552-f90e6acfd1bb","revision":"sha256:1eedf6bc5cb41d790969612edfe7fc38445dd7881a07fd67731d2a26b2657575","kind":"mcqs","content":{"question":[{"type":"text","content":"While accessing a term stored in a B+ tree in an inverted file index, range searchings are expensive."}],"options":[{"type":"text","content":"True","correct":false,"option_id":"d0ddbaea-d86d-4304-b5c8-4315057d0945"},{"type":"text","content":"False","correct":true,"option_id":"1ca068b4-5720-41a7-801d-634f4177a7b1"}],"explanation":[{"type":"text","content":"B+ 树按键顺序组织叶结点, 找到范围起点后可以沿叶结点顺序扫描, 范围查询是它的常见优势"}]}}},{"path":"versions/6c523b72-3540-451d-b2d9-519ead0d584b/5f9bc95907b66761c56ca90c74662dd350c839f576a64c16f3a838405b2638b5.json","value":{"schema_version":1,"revision_scheme":"holly-question-v1","bank_id":"3eb3811b-4425-46ad-8bb6-a0504dca151b","question_id":"6c523b72-3540-451d-b2d9-519ead0d584b","revision":"sha256:5f9bc95907b66761c56ca90c74662dd350c839f576a64c16f3a838405b2638b5","kind":"mcqs","content":{"question":[{"type":"text","content":"In a B+ Tree, an internal node with k children stores k−1 smallest key values in the subtrees except the first one."}],"options":[{"type":"text","content":"True","correct":true,"option_id":"226f1c15-6a6f-44bb-a6d6-b60f6cce7a21"},{"type":"text","content":"False","correct":false,"option_id":"a35476c2-d293-4cf0-a3fe-ea752a665d74"}],"explanation":[{"type":"text","content":"分隔键取各个非首孩子子树的最小键, k 个孩子对应 k−1 个此类分隔键"}]}}},{"path":"versions/04bbf3b6-b4c2-42f3-b6fb-9592df1768c5/7dff1854848b2d397a84a6ff4f5618de99b7b2c6e364b9cf32f6dd3b6d672c33.json","value":{"schema_version":1,"revision_scheme":"holly-question-v1","bank_id":"3eb3811b-4425-46ad-8bb6-a0504dca151b","question_id":"04bbf3b6-b4c2-42f3-b6fb-9592df1768c5","revision":"sha256:7dff1854848b2d397a84a6ff4f5618de99b7b2c6e364b9cf32f6dd3b6d672c33","kind":"mcqs","content":{"question":[{"type":"text","content":"Precision measures the quality of all the retrieved documents."}],"options":[{"type":"text","content":"True","correct":true,"option_id":"a3960874-2229-4110-90f4-e8659282ba10"},{"type":"text","content":"False","correct":false,"option_id":"196aaffb-6345-4f1d-b3c6-1b3602333b53"}],"explanation":[{"type":"text","content":"Precision 是检索结果中相关文档所占比例, 用来衡量返回结果的相关质量"}]}}},{"path":"versions/2a3bde6a-8fc3-421b-bc07-d4a97dcb02e3/ae61ce6761121b3bbcd69a2a522c9b202cb06d9a9c844c0febbf3559816e0ae3.json","value":{"schema_version":3,"revision_scheme":"holly-question-v1","bank_id":"3eb3811b-4425-46ad-8bb6-a0504dca151b","question_id":"2a3bde6a-8fc3-421b-bc07-d4a97dcb02e3","revision":"sha256:ae61ce6761121b3bbcd69a2a522c9b202cb06d9a9c844c0febbf3559816e0ae3","kind":"mcqs","content":{"question":[{"type":"text","content":"In a search engine, thresholding for query retrieves the top $k$ documents according to their weights."}],"options":[{"type":"text","content":"True","correct":false,"option_id":"eb16bfe2-83af-4451-96fa-e73e759309b9"},{"type":"text","content":"False","correct":false,"option_id":"374b4cdb-b955-458a-998e-e4b8ef70c275"}],"answer_status":"unavailable","selection_mode":"single"}}},{"path":"versions/e9004dcf-9642-4a99-bc1d-079744a3d288/bb4c504081279e3e901c9551862cc30d969d0d17437c19661aa08eb079e9ce12.json","value":{"schema_version":3,"revision_scheme":"holly-question-v1","bank_id":"3eb3811b-4425-46ad-8bb6-a0504dca151b","question_id":"e9004dcf-9642-4a99-bc1d-079744a3d288","revision":"sha256:bb4c504081279e3e901c9551862cc30d969d0d17437c19661aa08eb079e9ce12","kind":"mcqs","content":{"question":[{"type":"text","content":"In general, comparing with the terms with short posting lists,  those with very long posting lists are less important."}],"options":[{"type":"text","content":"True","correct":false,"option_id":"0bf64198-d7bb-4836-bb5f-db4974379871"},{"type":"text","content":"False","correct":false,"option_id":"4c462851-bb1b-44fc-95e7-2b78744b289a"}],"answer_status":"unavailable","selection_mode":"single"}}},{"path":"versions/95b9255e-f572-4b91-92e4-2799fc96f5ba/3f7a4f1c7c14f1fbff18530b3c25f2d7f52ebee91cbad4c96cc051f707d7a1b7.json","value":{"schema_version":3,"revision_scheme":"holly-question-v1","bank_id":"3eb3811b-4425-46ad-8bb6-a0504dca151b","question_id":"95b9255e-f572-4b91-92e4-2799fc96f5ba","revision":"sha256:3f7a4f1c7c14f1fbff18530b3c25f2d7f52ebee91cbad4c96cc051f707d7a1b7","kind":"mcqs","content":{"question":[{"type":"text","content":"Among the following groups of concepts, which group is not totally relevant to a search engine?"}],"options":[{"type":"text","content":"distributed index, backtracking, query","correct":false,"option_id":"07d83fb1-a217-4217-ae3f-e2e5f63f2e6c"},{"type":"text","content":"inverted file index, stop words, precision","correct":false,"option_id":"209e84cd-ba3c-4eef-a0ff-3dec50ba2dc6"},{"type":"text","content":"posting list, thresholding, recall","correct":false,"option_id":"06890263-27f5-4015-a402-9a07aade2d73"},{"type":"text","content":"word stemming, hashing, compression","correct":false,"option_id":"d8d8ba4b-20ba-4982-b66d-2d5188254735"}],"answer_status":"unavailable","selection_mode":"single"}}},{"path":"versions/9a5d9b84-9b93-420d-93f0-6009961163dd/69b22c9892f855f22e357bc5bd49b9ca2731779b1fc6bb7eceec990bcf5aab38.json","value":{"schema_version":3,"revision_scheme":"holly-question-v1","bank_id":"3eb3811b-4425-46ad-8bb6-a0504dca151b","question_id":"9a5d9b84-9b93-420d-93f0-6009961163dd","revision":"sha256:69b22c9892f855f22e357bc5bd49b9ca2731779b1fc6bb7eceec990bcf5aab38","kind":"mcqs","content":{"question":[{"type":"text","content":"Which of the following is NOT a step in the process of building an inverted file index?"}],"options":[{"type":"text","content":"Check dictionary with each term: if it is not in, insert it into the dictionary","correct":false,"option_id":"dc8eff84-235a-4fd0-b319-18153a482522"},{"type":"text","content":"Use stemming and stop words filter to obtain terms","correct":false,"option_id":"5a3fba83-178a-4501-b78a-75293fd05323"},{"type":"text","content":"Get the posting list for each term and calculate the precision","correct":false,"option_id":"4d9ded05-e329-4260-b36e-572363dba419"},{"type":"text","content":"Read in strings and parse to get words","correct":false,"option_id":"175ae88a-a1c7-4718-bed1-ab092cd08aad"}],"answer_status":"unavailable","selection_mode":"single"}}},{"path":"versions/a04d7c0c-a891-4b3e-8ca8-900ce839d525/7f9aede09de55dca5967c2d8a3ca8dee4dd9eae75729bac67c23869ed865da67.json","value":{"schema_version":3,"revision_scheme":"holly-question-v1","bank_id":"3eb3811b-4425-46ad-8bb6-a0504dca151b","question_id":"a04d7c0c-a891-4b3e-8ca8-900ce839d525","revision":"sha256:7f9aede09de55dca5967c2d8a3ca8dee4dd9eae75729bac67c23869ed865da67","kind":"mcqs","content":{"question":[{"type":"text","content":"Insert 3, 1, 4, 5, 9, 2, 6, 8, 7, 0 into an initially empty 2-3 tree (with splitting).  Which one of the following statements is FALSE?"}],"options":[{"type":"text","content":"the parent of the node containing 5 has 3 children","correct":false,"option_id":"18f62153-8976-441c-b3e9-467a1a59172c"},{"type":"text","content":"there are 5 leaf nodes","correct":false,"option_id":"ce49deeb-8743-457a-99de-a8ac1733f962"},{"type":"text","content":"7 and 8 are in the same node","correct":false,"option_id":"343ccca9-774b-47e1-9237-d4e5c5438721"},{"type":"text","content":"the first key stored in the root is 6","correct":false,"option_id":"61ab0a2c-6d67-4a23-b6b8-5a7bb82c8d8f"}],"answer_status":"unavailable","selection_mode":"single"}}},{"path":"versions/162a49f5-c664-4557-bbdb-59f60f486bfb/fc14166877d6f231fe7a99d7d2a7fbee9402f5bd08d36c5edad78746c97aefda.json","value":{"schema_version":3,"revision_scheme":"holly-question-v1","bank_id":"3eb3811b-4425-46ad-8bb6-a0504dca151b","question_id":"162a49f5-c664-4557-bbdb-59f60f486bfb","revision":"sha256:fc14166877d6f231fe7a99d7d2a7fbee9402f5bd08d36c5edad78746c97aefda","kind":"mcqs","content":{"question":[{"type":"text","content":"Two red-black trees are said to be different if they have different tree structures or different node colors.  How many different red-black trees are there with 3 internal nodes?"}],"options":[{"type":"text","content":"1","correct":false,"option_id":"a4543ba3-cf53-465b-b9c0-72cc2009f4d0"},{"type":"text","content":"2","correct":false,"option_id":"5e0765df-164d-4911-b0b8-4c0ce3098b35"},{"type":"text","content":"more than 3","correct":false,"option_id":"adb4739f-a024-4534-8888-74931e6d6af0"},{"type":"text","content":"3","correct":false,"option_id":"fb41b063-e857-4dc9-8923-9f0f4ad7fb99"}],"answer_status":"unavailable","selection_mode":"single"}}},{"path":"versions/b7806be6-cd3c-446e-ac60-3ff534f032a4/9c0870bb6a892fc34ff25f418bdb208f0378ceec98b72617fd45835917771b0a.json","value":{"schema_version":3,"revision_scheme":"holly-question-v1","bank_id":"3eb3811b-4425-46ad-8bb6-a0504dca151b","question_id":"b7806be6-cd3c-446e-ac60-3ff534f032a4","revision":"sha256:9c0870bb6a892fc34ff25f418bdb208f0378ceec98b72617fd45835917771b0a","kind":"problems","content":{"question":[{"type":"text","content":"The function FindKey is to check if a given key is in a B+ Tree with its root pointed by root. \n\nReturn true if key is in the tree, or false if not. The B+ tree structure is defined as following:"},{"type":"code","content":"static int order = DEFAULT_ORDER;\ntypedef struct BpTreeNode BpTreeNode;\nstruct BpTreeNode {\n    BpTreeNode** childrens;  /* Pointers to childrens. This field is not used by leaf nodes. */\n    ElementType* keys;\n    BpTreeNode* parent;\n    bool isLeaf;  /* 1 if this node is a leaf, or 0 if not */\n    int numKeys;  /* This field is used to keep track of the number of valid keys. \n    In an internal node, the number of valid pointers is always numKeys + 1. */\n};\n\n\nbool FindKey(BpTreeNode * const root, ElementType key){\n    if (root == NULL) {\n            return false;\n    }\n    int i = 0;\n    BpTreeNode * node = root;\n    while ([填空 1]) {\n        i = 0;\n        while (i < node->numKeys) {\n            if ([填空 2]) i++;\n            else break;\n        }\n        node = node->childrens[i];\n    }\n    for(i = 0; i < node->numKeys; i++){\n        if(node->keys[i] == key)\n            return true;\n    }\n    return false;\n}"}],"answer":[{"type":"text","content":"参考答案待确认"}],"response":{"fields":[{"id":"blank1","label":"第 1 空","kind":"text","blank":"[填空 1]"},{"id":"blank2","label":"第 2 空","kind":"text","blank":"[填空 2]"}]}}}}]}